==English==

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*pewH-}}
From {{etyl|la|en}} {{m|la|amputō||prune, cut away}}.  The original sense of pruning (a tree, etc.) became obsolete.  The OED<ref name="NED">{{R:Oxford English Dictionary|volume=I|page=295|column=2}}</ref> considers uses related to anything other than an animal limb to be figurative uses of the modern sense.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈæmpjʊteɪt/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-amputate.ogg|Audio (US)}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|obsolete}} To cut off, to prune. {{century|17|18}}
# To [[surgical]]ly [[remove]] a part of the body, especially a [[limb]].  {{century|17}}

====Related terms====
* {{l|en|amputation}} (''noun'')
* {{l|en|amputee}} (''noun'')

